      "side": 1,
      "message": "The implementation returns 0 if lookup failed.\n\n1. This comment should note the error value and the condition under which it is returned.\n2. The callers should check for this value if they care whether they have a valid mode VDO.\n3. I don\u0027t think that 0 (or any other 32-bit value) is an inherently invalid mode VDO. Right now, this function is only being used for TBT, and 0 would be an invalid TBT mode VDO. But it\u0027s a generic function, so it would be good if it worked for arbitrary SVIDs.\n\nFor that reason, I might lean towards something like\n\nbool pd_get_mode_vdo_for_svid(int port, enum tcpm_transmit_type type, uint16_t svid, uint32_t *vdo_out);\n\nhere, even if it\u0027s a little ugly. If we return the VDO directly, we\u0027ll have to worry that in the future, there might be some valid VDO with whatever in-band error value we chose.",
